# Rust CLI engineering

Apply when designing, modifying or reviewing command-line programs, including standalone development tools.

- Prefer clap 4 derive for non-trivial Rust CLIs; typed subcommands/options, help/version and explicit invalid-input handling.
- Stable exit codes and versioned machine-readable results for automation.
- Read-only checks; explicit, bounded writes and no silent repair.
- Test the actual binary, including negative cases and supported OS targets.
- No unverified release or runtime deployment.

